From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:44:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve none color components through parse, mix and
 serialization

rgb(), hsl() and hwb() with none components eagerly resolved into the
legacy srgb form, which cannot represent none. Computed values came out
as rgb(0, 0, 0), and color-mix carry-forward never saw the missing
components. With this patch:

- resolve_to_absolute keeps the none flags. rgb() stays legacy-tagged
  (specified serialization is still rgb(0, 0, 0) per WPT
  color-valid-rgb) but the flags survive; hsl() and hwb() skip the
  legacy tag entirely when any component is none.
- AbsoluteColor::to_css falls back to the modern form for
  none-carrying colors: color(srgb ...) for legacy srgb, and functional
  hsl()/hwb() (percent form) instead of the srgb conversion.
- The specified serialization differs per WPT: the Absolute wrapper
  writes legacy-with-zeros for rgb and number-form hsl()/hwb().
- Bare relative-color channel keywords (r, g, b, ...) carry a none
  origin channel forward instead of substituting 0; calc() still gets 0.
- mix_many skips the srgb conversion for none-carrying results, which
  would lose them.

Covers the none rows of WPT color-{valid,computed}-{rgb,hsl,hwb},
color-computed-relative-color and color-computed-color-mix-function.
